    "message": {
     "content": "**Yes, you should strongly consider taking it.** \n\nFrom a pure compensation and negotiation standpoint, this is an **exceptional outcome** and effectively at the top of Google\u2019s L6 band. \n\n---\n\n### The Financial Reality of the Updated Offer\n\nBy holding the equity grant at $1.08M and giving you a **$200,000 cash sign-on bonus**, Google didn't just replace your $200k of unvested Meta RSUs\u2014**they effectively allowed you to double-dip in Year 1**.\n\n| Component | Current Meta (IC6) | Final Google Offer (L6) | Difference |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Base Salary** | $240,000 | $240,000 | Match ($0) |\n| **Target Bonus** | ~$36,000 (15%) | $48,000 (20%) | **+$12,000** |\n| **Year 1 Equity (33%)** | ~$200,000 | $356,400 | **+$156,400** |\n| **Sign-on Bonus** | $0 | $200,000 | **+$200,000** |\n| **Year 1 Total Comp** | **~$476k \u2013 $526k** | **$844,400** | **+$318k to +$368k (+60%+)** |\n\n---\n\n### 4-Year Outlook (Baseline without stock growth)\n\nBecause of the $200k cash upfront plus Google\u2019s 33/33/22/12 vesting:\n\n* **Year 1:** **~$844,400** ($240k base + $48k bonus + $356.4k equity + $200k sign-on)\n* **Year 2:** **~$644,400** ($240k base + $48k bonus + $356.4k equity + Refresher #1)\n* **Year 3:** **~$525,600** ($240k base + $48k bonus + $237.6k equity + Refreshers #1 & #2)\n* **Year 4:** **~$417,600** ($240k base + $48k bonus + $129.6k equity + Refreshers #1, #2, & #3)\n\n**4-Year Baseline Average:** **~$608,000/year** (excluding any refreshers or stock appreciation), compared to your Meta run rate of ~$526,000/year. With standard annual refreshers added in Years 2\u20134, your actual average over 4 years will likely sit between **$630,000 and $680,000/year**.\n\n---\n\n### 3 Final Details to Confirm Before Signing\n\n1. **Sign-On Payment Structure:** Confirm whether the $200,000 is paid as a **single lump sum** within your first 30\u201360 days, or if it is split (e.g., $100k in Year 1, $100k in Year 2). *(A single lump sum in Year 1 is preferable).*\n2. **Clawback Terms:** Google sign-on bonuses typically carry a 1-year or 2-year prorated repayment clause if you leave voluntarily. Make sure you understand the vesting/repayment schedule.\n3. **Meta Bonus Timing:** Check when Meta\u2019s upcoming performance bonus pays out. If it is only a few weeks away, set your Google start date after the payout date so you don't forfeit it.\n\n---\n\n### Verdict\n\nA $200,000 sign-on bonus for an L6 PM is very rare and represents Google using its maximum discretion to close you. Further counter-offering is unlikely to yield more and risks goodwill. **Sign the offer.**",
